{% doc %}
  Collection page head (TE-6 AC1, AC13; TE-22 AC9, AC11; docs/ui-spec/collection.md §4,
  foundation §3.3, §5). Reads the global `collection`. No settings.

  A, no image: snippets/breadcrumb → snippets/page-title (h1 collection.title) →
  collection.description in `.rte`, max 65ch, on the white band.
  B, collection.image: `.page-banner` card under the dark header with breadcrumb and
  h1 on the image (dark layer 75% → 60%, white text ≥ 4.56:1 on any image). The
  image is the page's LCP element: eager, fetchpriority high, alt="" (the h1 on it
  already names it). Rendered without a crop: image_tag sets object-position from
  the focal point and CSS cuts it with object-fit. Uses collection.image only, never
  featured_image, so a product image does not become the banner.

  Description with an image: a short one (at most 168 characters of text, about
  3 lines of 56ch) sits on the banner from 48rem and under it below 48rem; it is
  rendered in both places and CSS shows one (display: none, so it is read once).
  A longer one always sits under the banner, never cut.

  Test hooks: collection-banner (root), collection-banner-image,
  collection-banner-description, and the hooks of snippets/breadcrumb and
  snippets/page-title (page-title-heading is the h1).

  Empty state: no collection (block used outside the collection template) → a
  hint in the theme editor, nothing on the storefront.

  Self-contained: callers must leave the body empty.

  @example
  {% block 'container', id: 'collection-banner' %}
    {% block 'collection-banner' %}{% endblock %}
  {% endblock %}
{% enddoc %}

{%- if collection == blank -%}
  {%- if request.design_mode -%}
    <div class="collection-banner__hint" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
      {{ 'blocks.collection_banner.placeholder' | t }}
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}
{%- elsif collection.image != blank -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign image_sizes = 'min(100vw, ' | append: settings.max_page_width | append: ')'
    assign has_description = false
    assign short_description = false
    if collection.description != blank
      assign has_description = true
      assign description_length = collection.description | strip_html | strip | size
      if description_length <= 168
        assign short_description = true
      endif
    endif
  -%}
  <div class="collection-banner collection-banner--image" data-testid="collection-banner" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
    <div class="page-banner">
      {% render 'image',
        class: 'page-banner__media',
        image: collection.image,
        width: 1920,
        widths: '360, 720, 1080, 1440, 1920',
        sizes: image_sizes,
        loading: 'eager',
        fetchpriority: 'high',
        decorative: true,
        testid: 'collection-banner-image'
      %}
      <div class="page-banner__content">
        {% render 'breadcrumb' %}
        {% render 'page-title', title: collection.title %}
        {%- if short_description -%}
          <div class="rte collection-banner__description collection-banner__description--overlay" data-testid="collection-banner-description">
            {{- collection.description -}}
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>

    {%- if has_description -%}
      <div
        class="rte collection-banner__description collection-banner__description--below{% if short_description %} collection-banner__description--mobile{% endif %}"
        data-testid="collection-banner-description"
      >
        {{- collection.description -}}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
{%- else -%}
  <div class="collection-banner" data-testid="collection-banner" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
    {% render 'breadcrumb' %}
    {% render 'page-title', title: collection.title %}
    {%- if collection.description != blank -%}
      <div class="rte collection-banner__description" data-testid="collection-banner-description">
        {{- collection.description -}}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:general.collection_banner",
  "settings": []
}
{% endschema %}
